Explanation of the change:

- We remove the old “lookahead‐only” `{{(?=else\}\})}}` rule (which only ever lit up pure `{{else}}` and could not handle `{{else if …}}`).
- We insert two new sibling modes immediately after the `{{#…}}` opener:
  1. An `else if` variant whose `begin` regex matches `{{ else if…` and which reuses `OPENING_BLOCK_MUSTACHE_CONTENTS` (so that “if” is highlighted as a built-in, parameters get their own modes, etc.).  
  2. A pure‐`else` variant that highlights the word “else” and nothing else.
- By doing it this way, a chain like  

    ```
    {{#if foo}}
      …
    {{else if bar}}
      …
    {{else}}
      …
    {{/if}}
    ```

  will now lex exactly the same as Ember/Glimmer does: both `if` and `else if` clauses are treated like “opening” tags, and `else` by itself still works as a fallback.
